---
extras: ["roads"]
title: Voronoi cells
---
Scatter seed points and give every tile to its nearest seed: the map falls into cells [[t:121-126 s:15]].

## The rule
1. Scatter seed points inside the map’s outer ring. The demo: 16 [[c08a:21-26]].
2. Every tile joins its nearest seed, by a chosen distance [[c08a:36-47]].
3. **Edge:** a tile inside the map’s outer ring whose right or lower neighbor belongs to another seed [[c08a:96-110]].
4. What the edges become:
   - `walls`, the talk’s: the edges are walls [[t:136-138 s:16]];
   - `roads`, our own rule: the edges are floor and the cells solid. A tile is also an edge when its lower-right neighbor belongs to another seed [[own]].

{% table label="The demo’s three distances" rowheads=true %}
* Distance
* Measures
* Talk says the edges come out
---
* Pythagoras
* a straight line [[own]]
* relatively smooth [[t:130]]
---
* Manhattan
* blocks north plus blocks east [[t:131-133]]
* sharp-edged, more man-made looking [[t:131-133]]
---
* Chebyshev
* the larger of across and down [[own]]
* somewhere between the two [[t:134-135]]
{% /table %}

